    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "11178ebb_a2bcb4cc",
        "filename": "BUILD.gn",
        "patchSetId": 5
      },
      "lineNbr": 1612,
      "author": {
        "id": 19099
      },
      "writtenOn": "2022-12-16T17:50:14Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I agree `SK_USE_PERFETTO_MACRO_OVERRIDES` might be a little wonky. My intent was to both describe how we\u0027re \"overriding\" (perhaps not the best term) our own standard tracing macros that route to `SkTraceEvent` (https://source.chromium.org/chromium/chromium/src/+/main:third_party/skia/src/core/SkTraceEventCommon.h;l\u003d212-308;drc\u003de3772d2cae13ed606403aee8783825840a0dbd94) to instead route to Perfetto, and also how this integration with Perfetto is (currently) distinct from the other `SK_USE_PERFETTO`.\n\nBut as it stands right now, this code really is too specific to the Android framework to be directly usable elsewhere. So we\u0027ll have to iterate in the future anyway, at which point we could reword the #define to be more general. So perhaps for now we should just be more specific that this is only for Android framework?\n\nPerhaps one of the following?\n- `SK_USE_PERFETTO_ANDROID_FRAMEWORK`\n- `SK_USE_ANDROID_FRAMEWORK_PERFETTO`\n- `SK_ANDROID_FRAMEWORK_USE_PERFETTO`\n\nUnfortunately we can\u0027t just simply gate on `#ifdef SK_BUILD_FOR_ANDROID_FRAMEWORK` because that captures weird edge cases (e.g. host mode builds) where this isn\u0027t supported.",
      "parentUuid": "e723d6ee_dfec64f4",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 1612,
        "startChar": 18,
        "endLine": 1612,
        "endChar": 49
      },
      "revId": "acd32b8d8e46574a4f7ce7d6ea1058cd986d591e",
      "serverId": "5086850b-e599-37d2-8ec8-ff16aeccbf02"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "1938e12d_a5ec9992",
        "filename": "BUILD.gn",
        "patchSetId": 5
      },
      "lineNbr": 1612,
      "author": {
        "id": 5255
      },
      "writtenOn": "2022-12-16T20:33:38Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "But we may somehow rework this to support other platforms? At that point, I assume we\u0027d want to use the same name, for simplicity?\n\nAnother option might be to have this be a second level macro - i.e. if both this flag and `SK_USE_PERFETTO` are set, we take this path. But I don\u0027t know how complex that is in practice.\n\nI don\u0027t have a strong preference for any of these, or a suggestion for something better.",
      "parentUuid": "11178ebb_a2bcb4cc",
      "range": {
